course: dictionary
lesson: 7259
title: A word for colour
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A pigment is a substance that gives colour to something. Context gives you the clues. «Chlorophyll is the green pigment of leaves» tells you that a pigment is a colour inside things, and that leaves are green because of one.
explain: The second meaning is about paint. A pigment is a coloured powder mixed with oil or water to make paint. Test it by putting your meaning in: «Early artists ground rocks and plants to make pigments» only makes sense if pigments are coloured powders.
explain: Look for the clue in «melanin is the pigment in human skin, hair and eyes». Melanin is a pigment, so it must be a colour. You can use the same check every time: swap in your meaning and see if the sentence still works.
fact: A pigment is a substance that gives colour to something.
fact: «Chlorophyll» is the green pigment that plants use to catch sunlight.
fact: «Melanin» is the pigment in human skin, hair and eyes.
fact: Paint pigments are coloured powders mixed with oil or water.
fact: Most colours in nature come from pigments, which soak up some colours of light and send back the rest.
exercise: «Chlorophyll is the green pigment of leaves.» What is a pigment? | A sort of water | A kind of sunlight | *A substance that gives colour to something | A type of leaf
exercise: Early artists ground rocks and plants to make pigments for paint. What are pigments here? | Drops of rain | Hard stones with no colour | *Coloured powders for making paint | Lumps of wood
exercise: «Melanin is the pigment in human skin, hair and eyes.» Which of these is a pigment? | Rain | *Melanin | Sunlight | A soap bubble
test: «Animal colours come in two kinds: pigments, which are coloured stuff in the body like paint, and structures.» What is a pigment like, according to this? | A soap bubble | *Paint | A bending ray of light | A puddle
test: «Most colours in nature are pigments, coloured chemicals that soak up some colours of light and send back the rest.» What do pigments do with light? | Turn light into sound | Make all light disappear | Only glow in the dark | *Soak up some colours and send back the rest
exam: «They think the dark pigment melanin may have helped frogs survive.» What does pigment mean here? | A plant that grows in water | *A coloured substance that gives colour to something | A small hopping animal | A dark cave
